> By the way, does anyone know whether it's possible to teleport a boulder 
> to a space where there's already one?

A quick examination of the code suggests it'll try random positions
until teleport.c:goodpos() returns true. For objects, it appears as
though destinations which already contain a boulder always have a
false goodpos(). 

In other words, it looks like it isn't possible to teleport *any*
object (including a boulder) to a space which contains a boulder.

Wizmode experimentation supports this probabilistically over a small
number of samples, though one obviously can't prove a negative this
way.


